sections:
  - title: Sleeping
    img: a-slapen.webp
    alt: Bedroom with a high and a low bed and a small wooden ladder
    text: |
      <p>The house sleeps a family of 5 or 4 adults. The large upstairs bedroom has a <strong>210x180cm</strong> bed and a cot. Downstairs, bedroom 1 has a <strong>210x140cm</strong> double bed. Bedroom 2 has a high bed and a low bed, both <strong>210x90cm</strong>.</p>
      <p><strong>Clean bed linen</strong> is provided. Bedding and a blanket for the cot (110x60cm) are not included.</p>
  - title: Cooking
    img: a-koken.webp
    alt: Kitchen with a long window looking out on the church of Hoorn
    text: |
      <p>The kitchen has everything you need for a delicious holiday. The essentials, of course: a dishwasher, fridge, hob and kettle. But also a microwave, toaster and Nespresso machine, plus all the utensils you need. A bottle of wine is always waiting for you, with tea and coffee for when you arrive. A high chair is available too.</p>
  - title: Bathroom
    img: a-sanitair.webp
    alt: Bathroom with round mirror and wooden washstand
    text: |
      <p>There is a bathroom with a rain shower and a separate toilet. The upstairs bedroom also has a small washbasin with tap and mirror. From May to October you can shower outside, cold or warm, or rinse your feet after a day at the beach. Also handy: a washer-dryer for a quick load of laundry.</p>
  - title: Garden
    img: a-tuin.webp
    alt: The garden with the house and terrace under the trees
    text: |
      <p>The garden offers plenty of privacy and lovely spots to enjoy the sun or the shade. Eat together at the large table with 8 chairs, or relax on the lounge sofa in the afternoon sun. There is a hammock, and around the outdoor fireplace you can sit sheltered until late. Outdoor games are provided, and of course a fishing net and a football. Mind the windows :-)</p>
      <p>You can park your car on site. Bikes go in the shed, where you can also charge an e-bike battery. Handy!</p>
  - title: Living
    img: a-leven.webp
    alt: Living room with dining table, bean bag and doors opening onto the garden
    text: |
      <p>The living area has a bright dining corner for 6 with a lovely view of the garden. The sitting area is a cosy nook to unwind in. There is fast WiFi, Ziggo TV (with Netflix, HBO etc. for subscribers) and a Sonos system to play your favourite music. You can enjoy the fireplace from both the dining and the sitting area. Books and games are provided!</p>
  - title: Location
    img: a-locatie.webp
    alt: Aerial view of Hoorn with the church, the dunes and the North Sea
    text: |
      <p>The house is in the lively village of Hoorn, with a few practical shops and cosy, good restaurants (see the bottom of this page).</p>
      <p>Next to the house stands the 13th-century <strong>church of Hoorn</strong>, the oldest building on the island. The bus stops in the Dorpsstraat near the church, so the house is easy to reach without a car or bike.</p>
      <p>Within a few minutes' walk you are in the beautiful <strong>Koegelwieck</strong> dunes and the lovely <strong>Hoornse bos</strong> forest, full of walking paths and remarkable bunkers.</p>
  - title: Surroundings
    img: a-omgeving.webp
    alt: The artwork De Streken in the Wadden Sea
    text: |
      <p>A 2 km walk or bike ride from Simmerhûs lies Terschelling's most beautiful <strong>North Sea beach</strong>, with the beach pavilion <strong>Kaap Hoorn</strong> run by our friend Joost. Open in summer and winter!</p>
      <p>Cycle or walk through the polder for a few minutes and you reach the <strong>Wadden Sea</strong>, with breathtaking views. The cycle path along the dike is beautiful and takes you past <strong>De Streken</strong>, an impressive artwork you can see and experience in summer. Cycle on towards the <strong>De Boschplaat</strong> nature reserve, a wonderful place to wander.</p>
      <p>For children, the playground at <strong>Restaurant Zonneweelde</strong> is a must, with a terrace right next to it. You can go horse riding at <strong>Terpstra</strong>. And behind the church there is a football pitch that regularly hosts a game of kaatsen, the traditional Frisian ball game.</p>
  - title: Shopping
    img: a-winkelen.webp
    alt: The shop Ben van Alles in Hoorn
    text: |
      <p>For presents, small groceries and anything else you can think of, walk to <strong>Ben van Alles</strong>. The <strong>Boltsjekoer</strong> bakery (which also serves lovely breakfasts) is close by too, and in Hoorn you can rent a bike at <strong>Terpstra</strong>. For a big shop, go to the <strong>Spar</strong> in Lies or the <strong>Jumbo (with off-licence)</strong> in Formerum. Across the road is the large <strong>Zeelen</strong> bike rental.</p>
  - title: Lunch, dinner and drinks
    img: a-lunch.webp
    alt: A restaurant with a terrace in an old building in Hoorn
    text: |
      <p>Hoorn has some lovely restaurants. Right next to Simmerhûs is restaurant and hotel <strong>Aest</strong>, recently opened and a culinary highlight. On the other side of the Dorpsstraat you will find tapas restaurant <strong>De Reis</strong>, and a little further on <strong>Zonneweelde</strong> with its large terrace and playground. Do look in at <strong>Flang in de Pan</strong> for a special culinary experience. We are very happy that <strong>Groene Weide</strong> recently reopened, with good coffee, a cosy restaurant and live music at weekends. A few kilometres away in Oosterend is the <strong>Eilandbistro</strong>, with delicious French cooking, and if you cycle on to the sea you reach the original beach pavilion <strong>Heartbreak Hotel</strong>. You can also walk there along the beach from Hoorn.</p>
  - title: Our island favourites
    img: a-favorieten.webp
    alt: Beach pavilion at sunset
    text: |
      <p>We are big fans of the <strong>ZandZeeBar</strong> on the beach at Formerum. The village of Formerum also has bar <strong>de Vijfpoort</strong>, the <strong>Boekenboer</strong> bookshop and the <strong>Wrakkenmuseum</strong> shipwreck museum. <strong>De Koffiemolen</strong> is very relaxed with small children, and around the corner at <strong>De Rustende Jager</strong> you can have a simple but tasty bite on the terrace, or play games inside when it rains.</p>
      <p>Midsland regularly holds a street market (buy <strong>De Sjouw</strong> for all island events and dates) and is a nice place to shop. <strong>De Koffiepot</strong> and <strong>Pura Vida</strong> are our regular haunts there.</p>
      <p>West has several good clothes shops, a surf shop and a Hema. Get coffee, sandwiches and island treats from our friends at <strong>'T Lokaal</strong>. <strong>De Walvis</strong> at the Groene Strand is a must, with an amazing view thrown in; a walk to the lookout point or along the beach is highly recommended. Interested in history? <strong>Museum 't Behouden Huys</strong> tells you all about our wonderful island!</p>
